# How To Work In This Devteam Workspace

This is a devteam-managed workspace. Do not treat this directory as a single
repository.

Workspace:

- Name: `{{WORKSPACE_NAME}}`
- Root: `{{WORKSPACE_ROOT}}`
- Config: `{{CONFIG_PATH}}`
- Default track: `{{DEFAULT_TRACK}}`
- Default feature: `{{DEFAULT_FEAT}}`

The machine-readable workspace model starts at `.devteam/config.yaml` and may
include shared registries plus lane files. This file is the agent onboarding
entrypoint.

## First Action

When entering this workspace, inspect the dynamic devteam context before making
changes:

```bash
node "{{DEVTEAM_CLI}}" workspace context --root "$PWD" --for codex --text
```

Then choose or confirm a track and optional feature:

```bash
node "{{DEVTEAM_CLI}}" track list --root "$PWD" --active-only --text
node "{{DEVTEAM_CLI}}" track context --root "$PWD" --set "<track>" --text
node "{{DEVTEAM_CLI}}" track context --root "$PWD" --set "<track>" --feat "<feat>" --text
```

For a compact run/worktree/evidence view after selecting a track or feature:

```bash
node "{{DEVTEAM_CLI}}" status --root "$PWD" --set "<track>"
node "{{DEVTEAM_CLI}}" status --root "$PWD" --set "<track>" --feat "<feat>"
```

If Codex/Claude skills are available, use `devteam-console` as the daily
workspace entrypoint and `devteam-status` for compact read-only summaries.

## Track Model

This workspace may contain multiple tracks, and each track may contain multiple
features. A session should bind itself to a track plus optional feature instead
of assuming a global active track.

Before editing code:

1. List or inspect available tracks.
2. Ask the user which track and feature this session should work on unless the
   request clearly names them.
3. Start or select a run for that track/feature scope.
4. Work only inside the worktrees belonging to that track, or only the feature
   worktrees when `--feat` is selected.

Prefer session-local selection:

```bash
node "{{DEVTEAM_CLI}}" session start --root "$PWD" --set "<track>" --text
node "{{DEVTEAM_CLI}}" session start --root "$PWD" --set "<track>" --feat "<feat>" --text
```

Do not use `track use` to mutate the workspace default when multiple sessions
may be active. Use `--set <track>` plus optional `--feat <feat>`, or
session-local `DEVTEAM_TRACK`/`DEVTEAM_FEAT`, instead.

